es → 50 G (no block)\n2. policyBasePremium: 3 runes → 60 G (block)\n3. policyBasePremium: 4 runes → 100 G (no block)\n4. policyBasePremium: 7 runes → 175 G\n5. policyBasePremium: 2 runes + 1 moonstone → 75 G (no block, different types)\n6. policyBasePremium: 3 runes + 3 moonstones → 120 G (two blocks)\n7. insuranceSum: sword + amulet → 1600 G\n8. insuranceSum: sword + 3 runes → 1750 G\n9. insuranceSum: two swords → 2000 G\n\n*pricing.spec.ts (modifiers & full quote premium):*\n10. computeQuote: empty item list → 5 G\n11. itemSurchargeTotal: cursed sword + amulet → 50 G curse surcharge scoped to sword's base premium\n12. computeQuote: amulet, 2-year customer → 59 G (loyalty threshold)\n13. computeQuote: sword enchantment 5 → 145 G (high-enchantment threshold)\n14. computeQuote: cursed sword enchantment 5 → 195 G (both surcharges)\n15. computeQuote: sword enchantment 4 → 115 G (no high-enchantment)\n16. computeQuote: 2 runes follow-up → 53 G (rounds 52.5 up)\n17. computeQuote: newcomer cursed sword → 165 G (integration example 1)\n18. computeQuote: long-standing customer's 2nd contract, cursed sword → 160 G (integration example 2)\n\n*claims.spec.ts (claim payouts & cap):*\n19. computeClaim: regular sword, 500 G damage → 400 G\n20. computeClaim: rune, 200 G damage → 100 G\n21. computeClaim: dragon sword, enchant 9, 1000 G damage → 400 G (both clauses, 50% wins)\n22. computeClaim: dragon sword, enchant 5, 800 G damage → 700 G (dragon only)\n23. computeClaim: steel sword, enchant 9, 1000 G damage → 400 G (enchant only)\n24. computeClaim: dragon sword, enchant exactly 8, 1000 G damage → 400 G\n25. computeClaim: sword+amulet dragon attack → 600 G total (deductible per item)\n26. computeClaim: two sword damages on two-sword policy → separate deductibles\n27. computeClaim: rejects when damages exceed policy's item count for a type\n28. computeClaim: cursed sword cap based on unmodified insurance value → 2000 G\n29. computeClaim: first 1500 G claim on 1000 G sword → 1400 G payout, 600 G remaining\n30. computeClaim: second 1500 G claim → 600 G payout, 0 G remaining\n31. computeClaim: rounds 350.5 G down to 350 G\n32. computeClaim: rejects damage entry for item not on policy\n33. computeClaim: rejects damage entry with unknown item type\n34. computeClaim: rejects damage entry with amount: -200\n\n*scenario.spec.ts (CLI-level integration):*\n35. runScenario: single empty quote → premium 5 G\n36. runScenario: schema example (amulet quote + claim) → correct shape\n37. runScenario: rejects unknown item type in quote\n38. runScenario: rejects claim referencing item not in policy\n39. runScenario: rejects claim with negative damage amount\n40. runScenario: two successive claims reduce remainingCap correctly\n\nTest List Phase Complete. Proceeding to Red phase with the first test.\n\nLet's begin Red phase for test 1."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01UMoLyyhmS2zSZw5HmarrVZ","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && export NODE_ENV=development && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -30"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":936,"output":1592,"cacheRead":33966,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":36494,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784917842328,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-c972e050-12b1-4972-bc60-1db93613bf33","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01UMoLyyhmS2zSZw5HmarrVZ","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinkin