e ternaries there, each mass 4 for the conditional + arithmetic, now replaced by simple invocations).\n\n## Refactoring Complete\n\n**Naming Evaluation**: `itemSurchargeTotal` already accurately reveals its purpose (summing multiple item-level surcharges). No rename needed.\n\n**Refactoring Applied** (Rule 3 — No Duplication):\n- Extracted the repeated `condition ? base * rate : 0` pattern into a single `amountWhen(condition, base, rate)` helper.\n- This pattern appeared 4 times across `pricing.ts`: curse surcharge, high-enchantment surcharge (both in `itemSurchargeTotal`), loyalty discount, and follow-up discount (both in `computeQuote`).\n- All 4 call sites now express the same underlying business rule — \"apply a percentage rate to a base amount only when some condition holds\" — through one named abstraction instead of four independent ternary expressions.\n\n**Mass Change**: `itemSurchargeTotal` mass 27 → 20 (delta -7), plus a one-time shared cost of 9 for `amountWhen`, which also simplified two additional ternaries in `computeQuote` (net effect across the whole file is lower total mass despite the small fixed cost of the new helper).\n\n**Tests**: All 13 tests passing, no regressions."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/pricing.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/pricing.ts\nPassing tests: 13\nRecent Green phase: `itemSurchargeTotal` now computes two independent surcharges and sums them: curse surcharge (50% of base item premium when item.cursed) and high-enchantment surcharge (30% of base item premium when item.enchantment >= 5), added together.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text",