purpose so far: sums damage amounts and subtracts a single deductible, returns a payout + a (currently hardcoded) remaining cap.\n- Assessment: `computeClaim` accurately and generically describes \"computing a claim result\" — it doesn't overpromise or hide behavior. This name still fits the current single-test intent well.\n\nDecision: **Keep current name** — it's appropriately generic for a function whose contract (given policy, damages, cap used → claim result) will grow, and it doesn't mislead."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01JeNGjhor9BFaByN2oEfex2","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claims.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":3782,"output":271,"cacheRead":10066,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":14119,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784919539422,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-6fd56576-7053-4aa7-92f4-85f6891159ce","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01JeNGjhor9BFaByN2oEfex2","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface PolicyItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\n\nexport const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: PolicyItem[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  capUsedSoFar: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const totalDamage = damages.reduce((sum, damage) => sum + damage.amount, 0);\n  const payout = totalDamage - DEDUCTIBLE;\n  return { payout, remainingCap: 0 };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919543505},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_014qZ7JDb7ibSCNimx7egR27","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && npx eslint src/claims.ts 2>&1"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":4310,"output":1008,"cacheRead":10066,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15384,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784919543505,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-716e2a4e-435f-481e-a155-1ea90cea8680","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_014qZ7JDb7ibSCNimx7egR27","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"(no output)"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919555744},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Tw5pNpFLKNX4sSrST4to81","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/pricing.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01NoxV1CzfrpzGcTg9AiBLoK","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/items.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":4452,"output":2862,"cacheRead":10066,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":17380,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784919555745,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-6bf61c14-6bcc-467c-8601-295b4dfc4fc6","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Tw5pNpFLKNX4sSrST4to81","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { Item, policyBasePremium, MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE } from \"./items.js\";\n\nexport interface QuoteItem extends Item {\n  material?: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE: Record<string, number> = {\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\nconst itemBasePremium = (item: QuoteItem): number =>\n  MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE[item.type] ?? COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE[item.type] ?? 0;\n\n// Applies `rate` to `base` only when `condition` holds, otherwise contributes nothing.\n// Shared by every conditional surcharge/discount in this file (curse, high-enchantment,\n// loyalty, follow-up) so the \"percentage applied when a condition is met\" rule lives once.\nconst amountWhen = (condition: boolean, base: number, rate: number): number =>\n  condition ? base * rate : 0;\n\nexport const itemSurchargeTotal = (item: QuoteItem, baseItemPremium: number): number => {\n  const curseSurcharge = amountWhen(!!item.cursed, baseItemPremium, CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const highEnchantmentSurcharge = amountWhen(\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n    baseItemPremium,\n    HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n  );\n  return curseSurcharge + highEnchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nexport const computeQuote = (\n  items: QuoteItem[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  isFollowUpContract: boolean\n): number => {\n  const policyBaseSum = policyBasePremium(items);\n  const itemSurchargeSum = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemSurchargeTotal(item, itemBasePremium(item)),\n    0\n  );\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBaseSum * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount = amountWhen(\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS,\n    policyBaseSum,\n    LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE\n  );\n  const followUpDiscount = amountWhen(isFollowUpContract, policyBaseSum, FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE);\n\n  const total =\n    policyBaseSum +\n    itemSurchargeSum +\n    firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n    loyaltyDiscount -\n    followUpDiscount +\n    PROCESSING_FEE;\n\n  return Math.ceil(total);\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919586776},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01NoxV1CzfrpzGcTg9AiBLoK","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface Item {\n  type: string;\n}\n\nconst BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM = 25;\nconst BLOCK_SIZE = 3;\nconst BLOCK_PRICE = 60;\n\nexport const MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 100,\n  amulet: 60,\n  staff: 80,\n  potion: 40,\n};\n\nconst isMainItem = (item: Item): boolean => item.type in MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE;\n\nexport const policyBasePremium = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  const mainItemsTotal = items\n    .filter(isMainItem)\n    .reduce((sum, item) => sum + MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE[item.type], 0);\n\n  const componentCountsByType = new Map<string, number>();\n  for (const item of items.filter((item) => !isMainItem(item))) {\n    componentCountsByType.set(item.type, (componentCountsByType.get(item.type) ?? 0) + 1);\n  }\n  let componentsTotal = 0;\n  for (const count of componentCountsByType.values()) {\n    componentsTotal += count === BLOCK_SIZE ? BLOCK_PRICE : count * BASE_PREMIUM_PER_ITEM;\n  }\n\n  return mainItemsTotal + componentsTotal;\n};\n\nconst INSURANCE_VALUE_BY_TYPE: Record<string, number> = {\n  sword: 1000,\n  amulet: 600,\n  rune: 250,\n};\nconst UNINSURED_ITEM_VALUE = 0;\n\nexport const insuranceSum = (items: Item[]): number => {\n  return items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + (INSURANCE_VALUE_BY_TYPE[item.type] ?? UNINSURED_ITEM_VALUE),\n    0\n  );\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919586776},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Step 1: Naming Evaluation**\n\n- Current name: `computeClaim`\n- Purpose so far: given policy items, damages, and cap used so far, sum damages, subtract a one-time deductible, and return `{ payout, remainingCap }`.\n- Assessment: `computeClaim` is appropriately generic for a function whose contract will grow (cap logic, per-item deductibles, validation) across future tests. It doesn't overclaim or mislead about current behavior.\n\n**Decision: Keep the current name** — it fits both the current minimal behavior and the intended future scope.\n\n**Step 2: Initial APP Mass**\n\n```typescript\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\n\nexport const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: PolicyItem[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  capUsedSoFar: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const totalDamage = damages.reduce((sum, damage) => sum + damage.amount, 0);\n  const payout = totalDamage - DEDUCTIBLE;\n  return { payout, remainingCap: 0 };\n};\n```\n\n- Constants: `100`, `0` (reduce seed), `0` (remainingCap) = 3\n- Bindings: `DEDUCTIBLE`, `policyItems`, `damages`, `capUsedSoFar`, `totalDamage`, `sum`, `damage`, `payout` = 8\n- Invocations: 0\n- Loops: `reduce` = 1\n- Conditionals: 0\n- Assignments: 0\n\n**Total Mass = 3(1) + 8(1) + 0(2) + 0(4) + 1(5) + 0(6) = 16**\n\n**Step 3: Apply Simple Design Rules**\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass):** All 19 tests currently pass; verified with `pnpm test`.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent):** Names (`totalDamage`, `payout`, `DEDUCTIBLE`) are clear. However, `remainingCap: 0` is a silent placeholder — nothing in the code signals that this is a temporary hardcode pending future cap logic, which could confuse a future reader (or the refactor subagent in a later cycle) into thinking `0` is a real computed value.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication):** None present — single small function, no repeated logic.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements):** `policyItems` and `capUsedSoFar` are currently unused, but they're required by the test's call signature (`computeClaim(policyItems, damages, 0)`) and are known to be needed for upcoming tests (cap exhaustion, item validation). Removing them would break the test and violate YAGNI in the other direction (they're already speculatively-but-correctly present because the API shape is settled by the test). Kept as-is.\n\n**Step 4: Refactoring Applied**\n\nAdded a clarifying comment on the placeholder return value (Rule 2 — Reveals Intent). No logic, names, or structure changed."},{"type":