me":"subagent","arguments":{"agent":"refactor","agentScope":"both","task":"Test file: src/claims.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claims.ts\nPassing tests: 3 (in claims.spec.ts; 21 total across the project)\nRecent Green phase: Added `reimbursementRate(item)` helper returning 0.5 when `item.enchantment >= 8`, else 1 (full). `computeClaim` now looks up the policy item matching the first damage entry's itemType (using `.find(...)!`), applies the reimbursement rate to each damage amount, sums, and subtracts a single 100G deductible. Note: the current implementation only looks at damages[0]'s item type to find the policy item -- this is a known simplification that will need generalizing once multi-item-type damage tests are added.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":1478,"output":601,"cacheRead":116958,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":119037,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784919686514,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-50b82075-0f10-455c-8543-9ec05208e7c9","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01YSoRTGXfT1XMzd1zXZabaf","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 21 tests still pass.\n\n## Naming Evaluation (First Priority)\n\n- `computeClaim`: clearly reveals purpose — computes a claim payout/remaining cap. Fits.\n- `reimbursementRate`: clearly reveals purpose — returns the applicable rate. Fits.\n- `item` (parameter inside `computeClaim`'s body, bound to `policyItems.find(...)!`): too generic — reads like it could be a damage entry or any item. Given the known simplification (only `damages[0]`'s type is matched), the name should communicate *which* policy item was matched and *why* (first damage entry).\n\n**Decision**: Renamed `item` → `matchedPolicyItem`, and extracted `damages[0].itemType` into `primaryItemType` to make the simplification's assumption (\"all damages share item type of the first entry\") visible at the call site rather than buried in a `.find()` predicate. Added a comment flagging the known limitation directly next to the code that embodies it (previously the caveat only lived in the Green-phase summary, not in the source).\n\n## APP Mass — Before\n\n```ts\nconst item = policyItems.find((policyItem) => policyItem.type === damages[0].itemType)!;\nconst totalDamage = damages.reduce(\n  (sum, damage) => sum + damage.amount * reimbursementRate(item),\n  0\n);\n```\n- Bindings: `item`, `policyItems`, `policyItem`, `damages`, `sum`, `damage` = 6\n- Invocations: `find`, `reduce`, `reimbursementRate` = 3 → 3×2 = 6\n- Loops: `find` (1), `reduce` (1) = 2 → 2×5 = 10\n- Constants: `0` = 1\n- Property access (`damages[0].itemType`) treated as bindings, not separately counted\n\nTotal: 6 + 6 + 10 + 1 = **23**\n\n## APP Mass — After\n\n```ts\nconst primaryItemType = damages[0].itemType;\nconst matchedPolicyItem = policyItems.find(\n  (policyItem) => policyItem.type === primaryItemType\n)!;\nconst totalDamage = damages.reduce(\n  (sum, damage) => sum + damage.amount * reimbursementRate(matchedPolicyItem),\n  0\n);\n```\n- Bindings: `primaryItemType`, `matchedPolicyItem`, `policyItems`, `policyItem`, `damages`, `sum`, `damage` = 7\n- Invocations: `find`, `reduce`, `reimbursementRate` = 3 → 6\n- Loops: `find`, `reduce` = 2 → 10\n- Constants: `0` = 1\n\nTotal: 7 + 6 + 10 + 1 = **24**\n\n## Mass Change\n23 → 24 (Δ +1)\n\n## Rationale (Rule 2 trumps APP)\nThe extra binding (`primaryItemType`) raises mass by 1, but it makes the simplification explicit and self-documenting: instead of an inline `damages[0].itemType` buried inside a predicate, the code now names the concept (\"the item type we're currently treating as canonical for this claim\") right where future readers/refactorers will need to generalize it for multi-item-type claims (per the `it.todo` for that scenario). Clarity wins over the 1-point mass increase.\n\n## Simple Design Rules Applied\n1. **Tests Pass**: ✅ 21/21 still passing, no regressions.\n2. **Reveals Intent**: Improved — `matchedPolicyItem` and `primaryItemType` are explicit about what they represent and why, plus an inline comment documents the known limitation directly in source.\n3. **No Duplication**: None found; no action needed.\n4. **Fewest Elements**: Not reduced (deliberately traded 1 unit of mass for clarity) — no unnecessary abstractions were removed or added beyond the naming/extraction above.\n\n---\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Renamed `item` → `matchedPolicyItem`, extracted `primaryItemType` explaining variable, added inline comment documenting the single-item-type simplification.\n**Mass Change**: 23 → 24 (+1, accepted per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 21 passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claims.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claims.ts\nPassing tests: 3 (in claims.spec.ts; 21 total across the project)\nRecent Green phase: Added `reimbursementRate(item)` helper returning 0.5 when `item.enchantment >= 8`, else 1 (full). `computeClaim` now looks up the policy item matching the first damage entry's itemType (using `.find(...)!`), applies the reimbursement rate to each damage amount, sums, and subtracts a single 100G deductible. Note: the current implementation only looks at damages[0]'s item type to find the policy item -- this is a known simplification that will need generalizing once multi-item-type damage tests are added.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claims.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claims.ts\nPassing tests: 3 (in claims.spec.ts; 21 total across the project)\nRecent Green phase: Added `reimbursementRate(item)` helper returning 0.5 when `item.enchantment >= 8`, else 1 (full). `computeClaim` now looks up the policy item matching the first damage entry's itemType (using `.find(...)!`), applies the reimbursement rate to each damage amount, sums, and subtracts a single 100G deductible. Note: the current implementation only looks at damages[0]'s item type to find the policy item -- this is a known simplification that will need generalizing once multi-item-type damage tests are added.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784919695038},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01AJK33CdQ46R1gonMFv8uas","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claims.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01P32QvTSs5FRKz3U6DdA8mQ","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claims.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":346,"output":114,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10228,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784919695058,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-f6f81430-4d74-4aa1-9049-953a8520201b","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01AJK33CdQ46R1gonMFv8uas","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface PolicyItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst FULL_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 1;\n\nconst reimbursementRate = (item: PolicyItem): number => {\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD) {\n    return HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return FULL_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n};\n\nexport const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: PolicyItem[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  capUsedSoFar: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const item = policyItems.find((policyItem) => policyItem.type === damages[0].itemType)!;\n  const totalDamage = damages.reduce(\n    (sum, damage) => sum + damage.amount * reimbursementRate(item),\n    0\n  );\n  const payout = totalDamage - DEDUCTIBLE;\n  // remainingCap is not yet computed -- no test exercises the cap logic yet.\n  return { payout, remainingCap: 0 };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919696585},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01P32QvTSs5FRKz3U6DdA8mQ","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { computeClaim } from \"./claims.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claims\", () => {\n  // Standard reimbursement (no special clauses)\n  it(\"computeClaim pays 400 G for a regular sword (steel, enchantment 3) with 500 G damage (full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible; no special clause applies)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }];\n    const damages = [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }];\n    expect(computeClaim(policyItems, damages, 0).payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"computeClaim pays 100 G for a rune (insurance value 250 G) with 200 G damage (full reimbursement minus deductible; runes have no enchantment level or material, so no special clause applies)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"rune\" }];\n    const damages = [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }];\n    expect(computeClaim(policyItems, damages, 0).payout).toBe(100);\n  });\n\n  // Enchantment threshold vs. dragon material\n  it(\"computeClaim pays 400 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G (both clauses apply; the 50% rule wins, then deductible: 500-100)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9 }];\n    const damages = [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }];\n    expect(computeClaim(policyItems, damages, 0).payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim pays 700 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G (only dragon-material clause: full reimbursement, then deductible: 800-100)\");\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim pays 400 G for a steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G (only high-enchantment clause: 50% first, then deductible: 500-100)\");\n\n  // Modifier thresholds (claim side)\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim pays 400 G for a dragon-material sword with exactly enchantment 8, damage 1000 G (high-enchantment clause applies, then deductible)\");\n\n  // Deductible per damage event\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim pays 600 G total for a dragon attack damaging an insured sword (500 G) and an insured amulet (300 G), deductible applied once per damaged item\");\n\n  // Multiple items of the same type\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim treats two damage entries of {itemType: sword} on a two-sword policy as separate damages, each with its own deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim rejects a claim (throws) when damages contain more entries of a type than the policy covers (e.g. two sword damages but only one sword insured)\");\n\n  // Cap exhaustion\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim caps a cursed sword's claim at 2000 G based on the unmodified insurance value of 1000 G (premium modifiers do not raise the cap)\");\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim pays 1400 G and leaves 600 G remaining cap for a first 1500 G claim against a 1000 G insured sword (cap 2000 G)\");\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim pays 600 G and leaves 0 G remaining cap for a second successive 1500 G claim against the same sword after the first claim already used 1400 G of the 2000 G cap\");\n\n  // Rounding in the MHPCO's favor\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim rounds a payout of 350.5 G down to 350 G\");\n\n  // Edge cases (validation)\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim rejects a claim (throws) when a damage entry references an item not part of the policy (e.g. amulet damaged when only a sword is insured)\");\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim rejects a claim (throws) when a damage entry references an unknown item type\");\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim rejects a claim (throws) when a damage entry has amount: -200\");\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919696585},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01GxpY47mToPuaRhiHC5hJfa","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -60"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":2421,"output":143,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":12332,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784919696586,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-68963ae1-3f51-48d3-8ea2-0f7d407f3fdb","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01GxpY47mToPuaRhiHC5hJfa","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/claims.spec.ts  (16 tests | 13 skipped) 2ms\n ✓ src/pricing.spec.ts  (9 tests) 3ms\n ✓ src/items.spec.ts  (9 tests) 2ms\n ↓ src/scenario.spec.ts  (6 tests | 6 skipped)\n\n Test Files  3 passed | 1 skipped (4)\n      Tests  21 passed | 19 todo (40)\n   Start at  19:01:39\n   Duration  525ms (transform 43ms, setup 