ent flagging the known limitation directly next to the code that embodies it (previously the caveat only lived in the Green-phase summary, not in the source).\n\n## APP Mass — Before\n\n```ts\nconst item = policyItems.find((policyItem) => policyItem.type === damages[0].itemType)!;\nconst totalDamage = damages.reduce(\n  (sum, damage) => sum + damage.amount * reimbursementRate(item),\n  0\n);\n```\n- Bindings: `item`, `policyItems`, `policyItem`, `damages`, `sum`, `damage` = 6\n- Invocations: `find`, `reduce`, `reimbursementRate` = 3 → 3×2 = 6\n- Loops: `find` (1), `reduce` (1) = 2 → 2×5 = 10\n- Constants: `0` = 1\n- Property access (`damages[0].itemType`) treated as bindings, not separately counted\n\nTotal: 6 + 6 + 10 + 1 = **23**\n\n## APP Mass — After\n\n```ts\nconst primaryItemType = damages[0].itemType;\nconst matchedPolicyItem = policyItems.find(\n  (policyItem) => policyItem.type === primaryItemType\n)!;\nconst totalDamage = damages.reduce(\n  (sum, damage) => sum + damage.amount * reimbursementRate(matchedPolicyItem),\n  0\n);\n```\n- Bindings: `primaryItemType`, `matchedPolicyItem`, `policyItems`, `policyItem`, `damages`, `sum`, `damage` = 7\n- Invocations: `find`, `reduce`, `reimbursementRate` = 3 → 6\n- Loops: `find`, `reduce` = 2 → 10\n- Constants: `0` = 1\n\nTotal: 7 + 6 + 10 + 1 = **24**\n\n## Mass Change\n23 → 24 (Δ +1)\n\n## Rationale (Rule 2 trumps APP)\nThe extra binding (`primaryItemType`) raises mass by 1, but it makes the simplification explicit and self-documenting: instead of an inline `damages[0].itemType` buried inside a predicate, the code now names the concept (\"the item type we're currently treating as canonical for this claim\") right where future readers/refactorers will need to generalize it for multi-item-type claims (per the `it.todo` for that scenario). Clarity wins over the 1-point mass increase.\n\n## Simple Design Rules Applied\n1. **Tests Pass**: ✅ 21/21 still passing, no regressions.\n2. **Reveals Intent**: Improved — `matchedPolicyItem` and `primaryItemType` are explicit about what they represent and why, plus an inline comment documents the known limitation directly in source.\n3. **No Duplication**: None found; no action needed.\n4. **Fewest Elements**: Not reduced (deliberately traded 1 unit of mass for clarity) — no unnecessary abstractions were removed or added beyond the naming/extraction above.\n\n---\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Renamed `item` → `matchedPolicyItem`, extracted `primaryItemType` explaining variable, added inline comment documenting the single-item-type simplification.\n**Mass Change**: 23 → 24 (+1, accepted per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 21 passing"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":3533,"output":1425,"cacheRead":10112,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":15070,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784919733984,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-bf8df49a-cc86-41fe-9e70-3fa5b0d97587","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":12254,"output":5071,"cacheRead":49528,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":15070,"turns":5},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919749014},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_012phbTofEHDgWLHfAjVrh18","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && export NODE_ENV=development && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -15; cat src/claims.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":3507,"output":153,"cacheRead":116958,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":120618,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784919749020,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-24