`DEDUCTIBLE` reference, `0` = 2\n- Loops: `find` (1) + `reduce` (1) = 2 → 10\n- Conditionals: 0\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass ≈ 6 + 2 + 8 + 0 + 10 + 0 = **26**\n\n**Refactoring Applied**: Extracted an explaining variable `rate = reimbursementRate(insuredItem)` inside `payoutForDamage`, and renamed `matchedPolicyItem`/`policyItem` to `insuredItem`/`item` for tighter, more domain-accurate naming (an item found on the policy that covers the damaged item is \"the insured item,\" not merely \"matched\").\n\n**Refactored Code Mass**:\n```\nconst payoutForDamage = (damage: Damage): number => {\n  const insuredItem = policyItems.find((item) => item.type === damage.itemType)!;\n  const rate = reimbursementRate(insuredItem);\n  return damage.amount * rate - DEDUCTIBLE;\n};\nconst payout = damages.reduce((sum, damage) => sum + payoutForDamage(damage), 0);\n```\n- Bindings: `payoutForDamage`, `damage`, `insuredItem`, `item`, `rate`, `payout`, `sum` = 7\n- Invocations: `find`, `reimbursementRate`, `reduce`, `payoutForDamage` = 4 → 8\n- Constants: `DEDUCTIBLE`, `0` = 2\n- Loops: `find` + `reduce` = 2 → 10\n- Conditionals: 0\n- Assignments: 0\n\nTotal Mass ≈ 7 + 2 + 8 + 0 + 10 + 0 = **27**\n\nMass Change: 26 → 27 (delta +1)\n\n**Decision rationale**: Rule 2 (Reveals Intent) trumps APP mass. The added binding (`rate`) costs +1 mass but converts an opaque inline expression (`damage.amount * reimbursementRate(matchedPolicyItem) - DEDUCTIBLE`) into a self-documenting three-step calculation (find insured item → get rate → apply rate and deductible), matching the shape of the domain rule described in the spec (\"full reimbursement minus deductible\", \"50% rule then deductible\", etc.). The renamed `insuredItem`/`item` also removes the redundant \"policy\" prefix already implied by the enclosing `computeClaim` scope, per Rule 4 (fewest/simplest elements without losing meaning).\n\nI evaluated further duplication (Rule 3) between `payoutForDamage` here and `itemBasePremium`/`itemSurchargeTotal` in `pricing.ts`, and the `isMainItem`/lookup pattern in `items.ts` — they operate on different domains (premium calculation vs. claim payout) with different formulas, so extracting a shared abstraction would reduce clarity for a superficial resemblance (both \"look up by type\"). No cross-file duplication extraction performed.\n\n---\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Renamed `matchedPolicyItem`/`policyItem` → `insuredItem`/`item` and extracted explaining variable `rate` in `payoutForDamage` for clarity (Rule 2 applied; function name `computeClaim` confirmed still fitting, no rename needed there).\n**Mass Change**: 26 → 27 (+1, accepted per Rule 2 > APP)\n**Tests**: All 25 tests passing (7 active in claims.spec.ts, 15 todo, no regressions). Lint clean."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/claims.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claims.ts\nPassing tests: 7 (in claims.spec.ts; 25 total across the project)\nRecent Green phase: Generalized `computeClaim` to compute a payout per damage entry (via a local `payoutForDamage` function that looks up the matching policy item by type, applies `reimbursementRate`, subtracts the fixed 100G deductible) and sums across all damages. This replaced the earlier version that only matched the first damage entry's item type and applied a single deductible to the whole claim.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/claims.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/claims.ts\nPassing tests: 7 (in claims.spec.ts; 25 total across the project)\nRecent Green phase: Generalized `computeClaim` to compute a payout per damage entry (via a local `payoutForDamage` function that looks up the matching policy item by type, applies `reimbursementRate`, subtracts the fixed 100G deductible) and sums across all damages. This replaced the earlier version that only matched the first damage entry's item type and applied a single deductible to the whole claim.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784919814740},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01XXrqXjCqgQ23Ztp69Ku4td","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claims.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Qb6pE4pPj1xfwkXb4gYm5R","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/claims.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":294,"output":116,"cacheRead":9768,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10178,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784919814765,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-6172ad0c-5c05-424d-86f6-f02e951b346f","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01XXrqXjCqgQ23Ztp69Ku4td","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"export interface PolicyItem {\n  type: string;\n  material?: string;\n  enchantment?: number;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n}\n\nexport interface Damage {\n  itemType: string;\n  amount: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nconst DEDUCTIBLE = 100;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD = 8;\nconst FULL_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE = 1;\n\nconst reimbursementRate = (item: PolicyItem): number => {\n  if ((item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_CLAIM_THRESHOLD) {\n    return HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n  }\n  return FULL_REIMBURSEMENT_RATE;\n};\n\nexport const computeClaim = (\n  policyItems: PolicyItem[],\n  damages: Damage[],\n  capUsedSoFar: number\n): ClaimResult => {\n  const payoutForDamage = (damage: Damage): number => {\n    const matchedPolicyItem = policyItems.find(\n      (policyItem) => policyItem.type === damage.itemType\n    )!;\n    return damage.amount * reimbursementRate(matchedPolicyItem) - DEDUCTIBLE;\n  };\n  const payout = damages.reduce((sum, damage) => sum + payoutForDamage(damage), 0);\n  // remainingCap is not yet computed -- no test exercises the cap logic yet.\n  return { payout, remainingCap: 0 };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784919816503},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Qb6pE4pPj1xfwkXb4gYm5R","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { computeClaim } from \"./claims.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Claims\", () => {\n  // Standard reimbursement (no special clauses)\n  it(\"computeClaim pays 400 G for a regular sword (steel, enchantment 3) with 500 G damage (full reimbursement minus 100 G deductible; no special clause applies)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 3 }];\n    const damages = [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 }];\n    expect(computeClaim(policyItems, damages, 0).payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"computeClaim pays 100 G for a rune (insurance value 250 G) with 200 G damage (full reimbursement minus deductible; runes have no enchantment level or material, so no special clause applies)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"rune\" }];\n    const damages = [{ itemType: \"rune\", amount: 200 }];\n    expect(computeClaim(policyItems, damages, 0).payout).toBe(100);\n  });\n\n  // Enchantment threshold vs. dragon material\n  it(\"computeClaim pays 400 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G (both clauses apply; the 50% rule wins, then deductible: 500-100)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 9 }];\n    const damages = [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }];\n    expect(computeClaim(policyItems, damages, 0).payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n  it(\"computeClaim pays 700 G for a dragon-material sword, enchantment 5, damage 800 G (only the dragon-material clause applies: full reimbursement, then deductible: 800-100)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 5 }];\n    const damages = [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 800 }];\n    expect(computeClaim(policyItems, damages, 0).payout).toBe(700);\n  });\n  it(\"computeClaim pays 400 G for a steel sword, enchantment 9, damage 1000 G (only the high-enchantment clause applies: 50% first, then deductible: 500-100)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", enchantment: 9 }];\n    const damages = [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }];\n    expect(computeClaim(policyItems, damages, 0).payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n\n  // Modifier thresholds (claim side)\n  it(\"computeClaim pays 400 G for a dragon-material sword with exactly enchantment 8, damage 1000 G (high-enchantment clause applies, then deductible)\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"dragon\", enchantment: 8 }];\n    const damages = [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1000 }];\n    expect(computeClaim(policyItems, damages, 0).payout).toBe(400);\n  });\n\n  // Deductible per damage event\n  it(\"computeClaim pays 600 G total for a dragon attack damaging an insured sword (500 G) and an insured amulet (300 G), deductible applied once per damaged item\", () => {\n    const policyItems = [{ type: \"sword\" }, { type: \"amulet\" }];\n    const damages = [\n      { itemType: \"sword\", amount: 500 },\n      { itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 300 },\n    ];\n    expect(computeClaim(policyItems, damages, 0).payout).toBe(600);\n  });\n\n  // Multiple items of the same type\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim treats two damage entries of {itemType: sword} on a two-sword policy as separate damages, each with its own deductible\");\n  it.todo(\"computeClaim re