AIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE` from items.ts + `COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE` in pricing.ts). If a new item type were ever added to pricing without updating scenario.ts's copy, the two lists would silently drift — a real conceptual duplication (single piece of knowledge: \"which item types exist\"), not just similar-looking code.\n\n**Refactoring Applied**:\n- Moved `KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES` into `pricing.ts`, computed as the union of the keys of `MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE` and `COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE` (the two tables that already define \"what types exist\"), and exported it.\n- `scenario.ts` now imports `KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES` from `pricing.ts` instead of maintaining its own copy.\n- This keeps the knowledge in one place (pricing.ts, where item-type pricing tables already live) without introducing awkward coupling — scenario.ts already imports from pricing.ts.\n\n**APP Mass**:\n\nBefore (scenario.ts):\n```ts\nconst KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\n  \"sword\", \"amulet\", \"staff\", \"potion\", \"rune\", \"moonstone\",\n]);\n```\n- Constants: 6 (string literals) = 6\n- Bindings: 1 (KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES) = 1\n- Invocations: 1 (new Set) = 2\n- Total: 9\n\nAfter (pricing.ts):\n```ts\nexport const KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\n  ...Object.keys(MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE),\n  ...Object.keys(COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE),\n]);\n```\n- Constants: 0 = 0\n- Bindings: 1 (KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES) = 1\n- Invocations: 3 (new Set, Object.keys x2) = 6\n- Total: 7\n\nMass change: 9 → 7 (delta -2), plus the elimination of a duplicated knowledge source (the real win here isn't the mass — it's removing a maintenance hazard).\n\n**Tests**: All 37 tests passing (3 todo, unaffected)."}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/scenario.spec.ts\nImp