8,"cacheRead":208463,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":210222,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784921869066,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-18eef2fd-2ffc-45b2-adca-53017fb9b2b3","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01239RnsqirWekzyhhHwDHR9","toolName":"subagent","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 41 tests pass. Here's the refactoring report.\n\n## Naming Evaluation (First Priority)\n\n- **Function**: `runQuoteStep`\n- **Purpose**: Runs a quote step, tracks per-step policy items, and determines follow-up discount eligibility.\n- **Assessment**: `runQuoteStep` still accurately describes the function's role — it hasn't gained new responsibilities that the name fails to capture. No rename needed.\n- **Variable**: `quoteStepsSeen` — clearly named, but redundant given `policyItemsByStepIndex` already tracks the same signal (see Rule 3 below).\n\n**Decision**: Keep `runQuoteStep`'s name. Eliminate the redundant `quoteStepsSeen` counter instead (see Rule 3).\n\n## Initial APP Mass (relevant excerpt)\n\n```ts\nlet quoteStepsSeen = 0;\n\nconst runQuoteStep = (step: QuoteStep, index: number): QuoteStepResult => {\n  assertKnownItemTypes(step.items);\n  policyItemsByStepIndex.set(index, step.items);\n  const isFollowUpContract = quoteStepsSeen > 0;\n  quoteStepsSeen += 1;\n  const premium = computeQuote(step.items, scenario.customer, isFollowUpContract);\n  return { premium };\n};\n```\n\n- Constants: `0` = 1\n- Bindings: `step`, `index`, `isFollowUpContract`, `premium` = 4\n- Invocations: `assertKnownItemTypes`, `.set`, `computeQuote` = 3 × 2 = 6\n- Conditionals: `quoteStepsSeen > 0` (comparison, counted as 1) = 4\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: `let quoteStepsSeen = 0`, `quoteStepsSeen += 1` = 2 × 6 = 12\n\n**Total Mass: 27**\n\n## Simple Design Rules Applied\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass)**: 41/41 passing before change — confirmed baseline.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Function name is fine, but having *two* separate pieces of state (`quoteStepsSeen` counter and `policyItemsByStepIndex` map) both tracking \"how many quote steps have happened\" obscures intent — a reader has to notice they're redundant.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Found conceptual duplication — `policyItemsByStepIndex.size` already tells us how many quote steps have been processed so far, making the separate `quoteStepsSeen` counter a duplicate source of the same knowledge. Removed the counter and derived `isFollowUpContract` from `policyItemsByStepIndex.size > 0`, computed *before* the `.set()` call for the current step.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: Removing the counter also eliminates a mutable `let` and an increment, reducing state and mutation surface.\n\n## Refactored Code\n\n```ts\nconst runQuoteStep = (step: QuoteStep, index: number): QuoteStepResult => {\n  assertKnownItemTypes(step.items);\n  const isFollowUpContract = policyItemsByStepIndex.size > 0;\n  policyItemsByStepIndex.set(index, step.items);\n  const premium = computeQuote(step.items, scenario.customer, isFollowUpContract);\n  return { premium };\n};\n```\n\n## Refactored APP Mass\n\n- Constants: 0 = 0\n- Bindings: `step`, `index`, `isFollowUpContract`, `premium` = 4\n- Invocations: `assertKnownItemTypes`, `.size` (property, not counted as invocation), `.set`, `computeQuote` = 3 × 2 = 6\n- Conditionals: `policyItemsByStepIndex.size > 0` = 1 × 4 = 4\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0 (no `let`/mutation left in this function)\n\n**Total Mass: 14**\n\n**Mass Change: 27 → 14 (delta −13)**\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n- **Duplication removed**: Eliminated the redundant `quoteStepsSeen` counter; `policyItemsByStepIndex.size` already carries this information.\n- **Mutation reduced**: Removed a `let` declaration and an increment (`+= 1`), lowering the assignment count to zero in this function.\n- **Naming**: Kept `runQuoteStep` — already accurate; no rename needed.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Removed redundant `quoteStepsSeen` counter, deriving follow-up-contract status from the existing `policyItemsByStepIndex` map size (Rule 3: No Duplication).\n**Mass Change**: 27 → 14 (delta −13)\n**Tests**: All 41 passing"}],"details":{"mode":"single","agentScope":"both","projectAgentsDir":"/home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking/.pi/agents","results":[{"agent":"refactor","agentSource":"project","task":"Test file: src/scenario.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/scenario.ts\nPassing tests: 7 (in scenario.spec.ts; 41 total across the project)\nRecent Green phase: Added a `quoteStepsSeen` mutable counter (initialized to 0 outside the step-processing closures) inside `runScenario`. In `runQuoteStep`, `isFollowUpContract` is computed as `quoteStepsSeen > 0` before incrementing the counter, then passed to `computeQuote` instead of the previous hardcoded `false`.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done.","exitCode":0,"messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Task: Test file: src/scenario.spec.ts\nImplementation file: src/scenario.ts\nPassing tests: 7 (in scenario.spec.ts; 41 total across the project)\nRecent Green phase: Added a `quoteStepsSeen` mutable counter (initialized to 0 outside the step-processing closures) inside `runScenario`. In `runQuoteStep`, `isFollowUpContract` is computed as `quoteStepsSeen > 0` before incrementing the counter, then passed to `computeQuote` instead of the previous hardcoded `false`.\n\nRefactor the implementation while keeping all tests green.\n\nRun autonomously, return when done."}],"timestamp":1784921875801},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_0148DFBCWczcttLwzYGQfLdH","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/scenario.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Sik1cgEbd7hnAugLmNT4k8","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/scenario.spec.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":10064,"output":116,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":10180,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784921875821,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-ed865000-d741-47b0-986c-13654cc5814e","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_0148DFBCWczcttLwzYGQfLdH","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { computeQuote, QuoteItem, KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES } from \"./pricing.js\";\nimport { computeClaim, PolicyItem } from \"./claims.js\";\n\nexport interface QuoteStep {\n  op: \"quote\";\n  items: QuoteItem[];\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStep {\n  op: \"claim\";\n  policy: number;\n  incident: {\n    cause: string;\n    damages: { itemType: string; amount: number }[];\n  };\n}\n\nexport type Step = QuoteStep | ClaimStep;\n\nexport interface Scenario {\n  customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: number };\n  steps: Step[];\n}\nexport interface QuoteStepResult {\n  premium: number;\n}\n\nexport interface ClaimStepResult {\n  payout: number;\n  remainingCap: number;\n}\n\nexport type StepResult = QuoteStepResult | ClaimStepResult;\n\nexport interface ScenarioResult {\n  results: StepResult[];\n}\n\nconst assertKnownItemTypes = (items: QuoteItem[]): void => {\n  for (const item of items) {\n    if (!KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES.has(item.type)) {\n      throw new Error(`Unknown item type: '${item.type}'`);\n    }\n  }\n};\n\nexport const runScenario = (scenario: Scenario): ScenarioResult => {\n  const policyItemsByStepIndex = new Map<number, PolicyItem[]>();\n  const capUsedByStepIndex = new Map<number, number>();\n  let quoteStepsSeen = 0;\n\n  const runQuoteStep = (step: QuoteStep, index: number): QuoteStepResult => {\n    assertKnownItemTypes(step.items);\n    policyItemsByStepIndex.set(index, step.items);\n    const isFollowUpContract = quoteStepsSeen > 0;\n    quoteStepsSeen += 1;\n    const premium = computeQuote(step.items, scenario.customer, isFollowUpContract);\n    return { premium };\n  };\n\n  const runClaimStep = (step: ClaimStep): ClaimStepResult => {\n    const policyItems = policyItemsByStepIndex.get(step.policy)!;\n    const capUsedSoFar = capUsedByStepIndex.get(step.policy) ?? 0;\n    const claimResult = computeClaim(policyItems, step.incident.damages, capUsedSoFar);\n    capUsedByStepIndex.set(step.policy, capUsedSoFar + claimResult.payout);\n    return claimResult;\n  };\n\n  const results = scenario.steps.map((step, index): StepResult =>\n    step.op === \"quote\" ? runQuoteStep(step, index) : runClaimStep(step)\n  );\n\n  return { results };\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784921877292},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Sik1cgEbd7hnAugLmNT4k8","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { runScenario } from \"./scenario.js\";\n\ndescribe(\"Scenario runner (CLI core logic)\", () => {\n  it(\"runScenario returns [{premium: 5}] for a scenario with a single quote step with an empty item list\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\" as const, items: [] }],\n    };\n    expect(runScenario(scenario)).toEqual({ results: [{ premium: 5 }] });\n  });\n\n  it(\"runScenario matches the schema example: amulet quote followed by a claim referencing policy 0, returning premium and payout/remainingCap\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 5 },\n      steps: [\n        {\n          op: \"quote\" as const,\n          items: [{ type: \"amulet\", material: \"silver\", enchantment: 2, cursed: false }],\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\" as const,\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: {\n            cause: \"fire\",\n            damages: [{ itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 200 }],\n          },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    const result = runScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result.results).toHaveLength(2);\n    expect(result.results[0]).toHaveProperty(\"premium\");\n    expect(result.results[1]).toHaveProperty(\"payout\");\n    expect(result.results[1]).toHaveProperty(\"remainingCap\");\n  });\n\n  it(\"runScenario throws when a quote step includes an item with an unknown type (e.g. {type: 'broomstick'})\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [{ op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"broomstick\" }] }],\n    };\n    expect(() => runScenario(scenario)).toThrow();\n  });\n\n  it(\"runScenario throws when a claim step's incident references a damage entry whose item is not part of the referenced policy\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\" as const,\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"amulet\", amount: 200 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(() => runScenario(scenario)).toThrow();\n  });\n\n  it(\"runScenario throws when a claim step's incident contains a damage entry with amount: -200\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\" as const,\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: -200 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    expect(() => runScenario(scenario)).toThrow();\n  });\n\n  it(\"runScenario processes two successive claims against the same policy, reducing remainingCap correctly across steps (1400 G then 600 G payout, as in the cap exhaustion example)\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 0 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"sword\" }] },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\" as const,\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"fire\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }] },\n        },\n        {\n          op: \"claim\" as const,\n          policy: 0,\n          incident: { cause: \"flood\", damages: [{ itemType: \"sword\", amount: 1500 }] },\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    const result = runScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ payout: 1400, remainingCap: 600 });\n    expect(result.results[2]).toEqual({ payout: 600, remainingCap: 0 });\n  });\n\n  it(\"runScenario returns 160 G for a long-standing customer's second quote step in the same scenario (integration example: first-insurance still applies, follow-up discount also applies)\", () => {\n    const scenario = {\n      customer: { yearsWithMHPCO: 3 },\n      steps: [\n        { op: \"quote\" as const, items: [{ type: \"amulet\" }] },\n        {\n          op: \"quote\" as const,\n          items: [{ type: \"sword\", material: \"steel\", cursed: true, enchantment: 7 }],\n        },\n      ],\n    };\n    const result = runScenario(scenario);\n    expect(result.results[1]).toEqual({ premium: 160 });\n  });\n});\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784921877292},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01MPbsqr4BhUzEu2vEYPjJ9Q","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"src/pricing.ts"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Q6BUXvN4VuBsQDvt3Ag2Dw","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":2681,"output":279,"cacheRead":10062,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":13022,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784921877293,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-0a283e59-1b4b-4771-bd9c-5784bd0f34ce","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01MPbsqr4BhUzEu2vEYPjJ9Q","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import { Item, policyBasePremium, MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE } from \"./items.js\";\n\nexport interface QuoteItem extends Item {\n  material?: string;\n  cursed?: boolean;\n  enchantment?: number;\n}\n\nexport interface Customer {\n  yearsWithMHPCO: number;\n}\n\nconst PROCESSING_FEE = 5;\nconst CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.5;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.3;\nconst HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD = 5;\nconst FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE = 0.1;\nconst LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.2;\nconst LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS = 2;\nconst FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE = 0.15;\n\nconst COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE: Record<string, number> = {\n  rune: 25,\n  moonstone: 25,\n};\n\n// The full set of item types this system recognizes at all -- the union of every\n// type that has a base premium (main item or component). Single source of truth\n// so callers don't need to know which table an item type lives in.\nexport const KNOWN_ITEM_TYPES = new Set([\n  ...Object.keys(MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE),\n  ...Object.keys(COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE),\n]);\n\nconst itemBasePremium = (item: QuoteItem): number =>\n  MAIN_ITEM_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE[item.type] ?? COMPONENT_BASE_PREMIUM_BY_TYPE[item.type] ?? 0;\n\n// Applies `rate` to `base` only when `condition` holds, otherwise contributes nothing.\n// Shared by every conditional surcharge/discount in this file (curse, high-enchantment,\n// loyalty, follow-up) so the \"percentage applied when a condition is met\" rule lives once.\nconst amountWhen = (condition: boolean, base: number, rate: number): number =>\n  condition ? base * rate : 0;\n\nexport const itemSurchargeTotal = (item: QuoteItem, baseItemPremium: number): number => {\n  const curseSurcharge = amountWhen(!!item.cursed, baseItemPremium, CURSE_SURCHARGE_RATE);\n  const highEnchantmentSurcharge = amountWhen(\n    (item.enchantment ?? 0) >= HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_THRESHOLD,\n    baseItemPremium,\n    HIGH_ENCHANTMENT_SURCHARGE_RATE\n  );\n  return curseSurcharge + highEnchantmentSurcharge;\n};\n\nexport const computeQuote = (\n  items: QuoteItem[],\n  customer: Customer,\n  isFollowUpContract: boolean\n): number => {\n  const policyBaseSum = policyBasePremium(items);\n  const itemSurchargeSum = items.reduce(\n    (sum, item) => sum + itemSurchargeTotal(item, itemBasePremium(item)),\n    0\n  );\n  const firstInsuranceSurcharge = policyBaseSum * FIRST_INSURANCE_SURCHARGE_RATE;\n  const loyaltyDiscount = amountWhen(\n    customer.yearsWithMHPCO >= LOYALTY_THRESHOLD_YEARS,\n    policyBaseSum,\n    LOYALTY_DISCOUNT_RATE\n  );\n  const followUpDiscount = amountWhen(isFollowUpContract, policyBaseSum, FOLLOW_UP_DISCOUNT_RATE);\n\n  const total =\n    policyBaseSum +\n    itemSurchargeSum +\n    firstInsuranceSurcharge -\n    loyaltyDiscount -\n    followUpDiscount +\n    PROCESSING_FEE;\n\n  return Math.ceil(total);\n};\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784921882055},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"toolu_vrtx_01Q6BUXvN4VuBsQDvt3Ag2Dw","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\n> tdd-experiment-run@ test /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n> vitest run\n\n\n RUN  v1.6.1 /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking\n\n ✓ src/claims.spec.ts  (16 tests) 4ms\n ✓ src/scenario.spec.ts  (7 tests) 4ms\n ✓ src/pricing.spec.ts  (9 tests) 3ms\n ✓ src/items.spec.ts  (9 tests) 3ms\n\n Test Files  4 passed (4)\n      Tests  41 passed (41)\n   Start at  19:38:01\n   Duration  563ms (transform 55ms, setup 0ms, collect 72ms, tests 14ms, environment 1ms, prepare 175ms)\n\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1784921882055},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_016P75qzo7pW7Nh87