ts: `0` = 1\n- Bindings: `step`, `index`, `isFollowUpContract`, `premium` = 4\n- Invocations: `assertKnownItemTypes`, `.set`, `computeQuote` = 3 × 2 = 6\n- Conditionals: `quoteStepsSeen > 0` (comparison, counted as 1) = 4\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: `let quoteStepsSeen = 0`, `quoteStepsSeen += 1` = 2 × 6 = 12\n\n**Total Mass: 27**\n\n## Simple Design Rules Applied\n\n- **Rule 1 (Tests Pass)**: 41/41 passing before change — confirmed baseline.\n- **Rule 2 (Reveals Intent)**: Function name is fine, but having *two* separate pieces of state (`quoteStepsSeen` counter and `policyItemsByStepIndex` map) both tracking \"how many quote steps have happened\" obscures intent — a reader has to notice they're redundant.\n- **Rule 3 (No Duplication)**: Found conceptual duplication — `policyItemsByStepIndex.size` already tells us how many quote steps have been processed so far, making the separate `quoteStepsSeen` counter a duplicate source of the same knowledge. Removed the counter and derived `isFollowUpContract` from `policyItemsByStepIndex.size > 0`, computed *before* the `.set()` call for the current step.\n- **Rule 4 (Fewest Elements)**: Removing the counter also eliminates a mutable `let` and an increment, reducing state and mutation surface.\n\n## Refactored Code\n\n```ts\nconst runQuoteStep = (step: QuoteStep, index: number): QuoteStepResult => {\n  assertKnownItemTypes(step.items);\n  const isFollowUpContract = policyItemsByStepIndex.size > 0;\n  policyItemsByStepIndex.set(index, step.items);\n  const premium = computeQuote(step.items, scenario.customer, isFollowUpContract);\n  return { premium };\n};\n```\n\n## Refactored APP Mass\n\n- Constants: 0 = 0\n- Bindings: `step`, `index`, `isFollowUpContract`, `premium` = 4\n- Invocations: `assertKnownItemTypes`, `.size` (property, not counted as invocation), `.set`, `computeQuote` = 3 × 2 = 6\n- Conditionals: `policyItemsByStepIndex.size > 0` = 1 × 4 = 4\n- Loops: 0\n- Assignments: 0 (no `let`/mutation left in this function)\n\n**Total Mass: 14**\n\n**Mass Change: 27 → 14 (delta −13)**\n\n## Refactoring Applied\n\n- **Duplication removed**: Eliminated the redundant `quoteStepsSeen` counter; `policyItemsByStepIndex.size` already carries this information.\n- **Mutation reduced**: Removed a `let` declaration and an increment (`+= 1`), lowering the assignment count to zero in this function.\n- **Naming**: Kept `runQuoteStep` — already accurate; no rename needed.\n\nRefactoring Complete:\n**Refactoring**: Removed redundant `quoteStepsSeen` counter, deriving follow-up-contract status from the existing `policyItemsByStepIndex` map size (Rule 3: No Duplication).\n**Mass Change**: 27 → 14 (delta −13)\n**Tests**: All 41 passing"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":6577,"output":1642,"cacheRead":10062,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":18281,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1784921973695,"responseId":"rqsty-cmpl-5e949e04-7971-44dd-9e25-e083028f7ae9","responseModel":"claude-sonnet-5"}],"stderr":"","usage":{"input":45959,"output":11659,"cacheRead":39954,"cacheWrite":0,"cost":0,"contextTokens":18281,"turns":6},"model":"requesty/vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","stopReason":"stop"}]},"isError":false,"timestamp":1784921989666},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_vrtx_01KKdEudd2LQrJ31grAPyJXG","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /home/experimenter/experiments/runs/2026-07-24_18-00-09_claim-office-example-mapping_v6.2-with-why-cleaned-pi_sonnet-5-no-thinking && export NODE_ENV=development && pnpm test 2>&1 | tail -15; cat src/scenario.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"requesty","model":"vertex/claude-sonnet-5@eu","usage":{"input":3404,"output":154,"cacheRead":208463,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":212021,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1784921